User Guide

Introduction
This prototype is a small banking application made in Windows Forms. It allows the user to
manage customer records and also manage different account types for each customer. The main
functions include adding customers, creating accounts, deposit, withdraw, transfer between
accounts, adding interest, and saving data when the program closes.
This guide explains the basic steps for using the prototype.

Main Features
The main features of the banking prototype are:
● add a new customer
● update customer details
● delete a customer
● open the account management form
● create Everyday, Investment, and Omni accounts
● deposit money
● withdraw money
● transfer money between the customer’s own accounts
● add interest where applicable
● save and load data using XML

How to Use the Prototype
1. Open the application
Start the program from Visual Studio or from the built application file. The main form will open
first.

2. Add a customer
In the main form, enter the customer number, customer name, and contact details. Tick the
bank staff checkbox if the customer is a staff member. Then click the Add button.
This will add the customer into the grid on the right side.

3. Update or delete a customer
Select a customer from the grid. The details will load into the input boxes. Change the details
and click Update to save the changes. Click Delete if you want to remove the selected customer.

4. Open account management
Select a customer and click Manage Accounts. This opens the second form for account actions.
5. Add an account
In the Manage Accounts form, choose the account type from the dropdown list. Enter the
opening balance and click Add Account.
The new account will appear in the accounts grid.

6. Deposit money
Select an account from the grid. Enter the amount in the amount box and click Deposit. The
account balance will update and a result message will show at the bottom.

7. Withdraw money
Select an account from the grid. Enter the amount and click Withdraw. If the withdrawal is valid,
the balance will reduce. If it fails, the message will show the reason and fee if appicable.

8. Transfer money
Select the source account in the grid. Then choose the target account from the target
dropdown. Enter the transfer amount and click Transfer.
If the transfer is valid, the money will move from the source account to the target account. If it
fails, the transfer will not complete and the fee rule may apply depending on the account type
and staff status.

9. Add interest
Select an account and click Add Interest. Interest is only added when the account meets its rule.
Everyday account does not add interest.

10. Close and reopen the app
When the application closes, customer and account data are saved automatically. When the app
is opened again, the saved data is loaded back.
